
4) After first login — this is a Fly Pi V3 KIAUH image
-------------------------------------------------------
KIAUH is already on the card under /opt/fly-kiauh. Klipper, Moonraker,
Fluidd, Mainsail, and Crowsnest are not installed. Use KIAUH to add them
after you log in.

Do not install Simple-AF (pellcorp) on this card.
Ignore any Simple-AF INSTALL_CMD / boot-display / GrumpyScreen / AUTO_CAMERAS
notes. This image's fly-start.txt is Wi-Fi, accounts, SERIAL_CONSOLE, and
SPI_DEVICE.

SSH in as the user you created, then:

  fly-kiauh
  # same as:  ~/kiauh/kiauh.sh

First boot copies KIAUH into ~/kiauh so it is owned by you. Do not run it
from /opt/fly-kiauh (that tree is root-owned).

The panel and the ADXL header share SPI. SPI_DEVICE in fly-start.txt picks
one. The change applies on the next boot.
